<title>SINGAPORE: Informatics announces board changes.</title>
<headline>Informatics announces board changes.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer training company Informatics Holdings Ltd said on Friday that Wong Tai had resigned as managing director.</p>
<p>Ong Boon Kheng had been appointed in his place.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement Wong Tai would remain as chief executive director and chairman of the board.</p>
<p>Wong Kock Meng, a director of the company, had been appointed deputy managing director. Cheah Hon Kuen, another director had been apointed vice chairman of the board.</p>
<p>All the changes occurred on February 27.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
